---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import AiLandingHero from '../../components/AiLandingHero.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { describeServiceHref } from '../../data/contact';

const context = 'AI for citizen access';
const mcpDocsHref = 'https://docs.registrystack.org/configure/breg-mcp/';
---

<Base
  title="Citizen access through an AI assistant | Registry Stack"
  description="Let people prepare a registry correction in chat, then review and submit it on your service website. Explore an experimental integration for selected tasks."
>
  <SiteHeader current="ai-citizen-access" />
  <main>
    <AiLandingHero
      eyebrow="AI for citizen access"
      heading="Help people start a registry request in chat."
      lead="Give people a guided way to prepare a correction with an approved assistant. They review and submit the request on your service website."
      context={context}
      exampleHref="#correction-example"
      exampleLabel="See the address example"
      note="Experimental integration with Base Registry Engine."
    >
      <div class="assistant-preview">
        <p class="ai-example-label">Approved assistant · Alex signed in</p>
        <p class="question-bubble">“Can I update my contact address?”</p>
        <p class="reply-bubble">“Your draft is ready to review on the service website.”</p>
      </div>
      <p class="handoff-label"><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span> Review link</p>
      <div class="review-preview">
        <div class="review-heading">
          <p class="ai-example-label">Service website</p>
          <span class="draft-label">Draft</span>
        </div>
        <p class="ai-example-title">Review address change</p>
        <dl class="address-fields">
          <div><dt>Current</dt><dd>6 Station Road</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Proposed</dt><dd>18 Market Street</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </AiLandingHero>

    <section class="section section-muted" id="correction-example" aria-labelledby="example-title">
      <div class="section-inner approach-split">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">Illustrative address correction</p>
          <h2 id="example-title">From a conversation to an official request</h2>
          <p>Alex has moved and needs to correct a contact address. After signing in, Alex can describe the change to the approved assistant and prepare a draft using the details the register permits.</p>
          <p>Alex signs in separately on the institution’s website to check the draft and choose whether to submit it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="editorial-callout">
          <h3>What Alex can do</h3>
          <ol class="approach-steps">
            <li><strong>Prepare the change</strong><span>Confirm the new address and get a link to the draft.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Review and submit</strong><span>Compare the proposed address with the current record on the service website.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Check progress</strong><span>After submitting, ask the assistant for the status if the institution has enabled that option.</span></li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="fit-title">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2 id="fit-title">Add an assistant for one task at a time</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="value-grid">
          <article>
            <h3>Keep your existing routes open</h3>
            <p>People can continue using your portal or another supported route. The configured service can run without an AI model.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>Choose the task and the details it needs</h3>
            <p>Approve the assistant, the fields it can read and the changes it can help draft. The register checks access when it receives a request.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>Keep review under your rules</h3>
            <p>Your institution decides who reviews the request. The register checks that the person or service applying an approved change has permission.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <p class="section-note">For technical teams, the <a href={mcpDocsHref}>Model Context Protocol (MCP) integration guide</a> covers sign-in, the separate service that grants access to each draft, and the review website. See also <a href="/architecture/headless/">how Registry Stack connects to your existing interfaces</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="final-cta" aria-labelledby="next-title">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <h2 id="next-title">Choose a request people can try</h2>
        <p>Tell us which task people need help with, which details it needs, and where they should review the draft. We’ll discuss how to evaluate it with your team.</p>
        <div class="section-links">
          <a class="button button-primary" href={describeServiceHref(context)} data-journey="service-inquiry">Discuss your service</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="/pricing/">View implementation options</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</Base>

<style>
  .assistant-preview, .review-preview {
    background: var(--registry-white);
    border: 1px solid var(--registry-paper-rule);
    border-radius: 5px;
    padding: 14px;
  }
  .question-bubble, .reply-bubble {
    border-radius: 4px;
    color: var(--registry-ink);
    font-size: var(--type-body-sm);
    line-height: 1.45;
    padding: 8px 10px;
    width: fit-content;
  }
  .question-bubble { background: var(--registry-blue-tint); margin: 10px 0 8px auto; }
  .reply-bubble { background: var(--registry-paper); margin: 0; }
  .handoff-label {
    color: var(--registry-blue);
    font: 600 var(--type-xs)/1.5 var(--registry-mono);
    margin: 8px 0 8px 14px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .handoff-label span { margin-inline-end: 4px; }
  .review-preview { margin-inline-start: clamp(8px, 2vw, 24px); }
  .review-heading { align-items: baseline; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px 10px; justify-content: space-between; }
  .draft-label {
    background: var(--registry-stamp-tint);
    color: var(--registry-stamp);
    font: 600 var(--type-xs)/1.5 var(--registry-mono);
    padding: 2px 6px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .review-preview .ai-example-title { margin: 6px 0 12px; }
  .address-fields {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--registry-paper-rule);
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px 16px;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    margin: 0;
    padding-top: 10px;
  }
  .address-fields dt { color: var(--registry-muted); font-size: var(--type-base); }
  .address-fields dd { color: var(--registry-ink); font-size: var(--type-body-sm); font-weight: 600; margin: 2px 0 0; }
</style>
